# Accessibility register (synthetic)
# GENERATED by scripts/provision_synthetic_sources.py -- do not hand-edit.
#
# 59 questions, and the highest-consequence family in the bank: getting an accessibility answer wrong strands a person. Some features are deliberately left UNVERIFIED so the hard filter is exercised in both directions - a register where everything is verified cannot test the rule that unverified is not accessible.
#
# EVERY record here declares ontosage:isSimulated true. This is DECLARED simulation,
# not fabrication: answers resting on it say so, and the scorecard reports the
# real/synthetic share. Replace with a real feed by pointing the same source kind at
# the institutional system -- the graph shape does not change.
#
# Deliberately imperfect: some assets are out of service and some accessibility
# features are unverified. A building where everything works would make the hard
# filter and the freshness gate untestable.

@prefix bldg: <http://abacwsbuilding.cardiff.ac.uk/abacws#> .
@prefix brick: <https://brickschema.org/schema/Brick#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ontosage: <http://ontosage.org/capabilities#> .

bldg:access_accessible_wc_0 a ontosage:AccessibilityFeature ;
    rdfs:label "Accessible WC - Floor 0 (Ground Floor)"@en ;
    ontosage:accessibilityKind "accessible_wc" ;
    ontosage:locatedIn bldg:Floor0 ;
    ontosage:layTerms "accessible toilet, disabled toilet, wheelchair toilet" ;
    ontosage:accessibilityVerified true ;
    ontosage:accessibilityVerifiedOn "2025-12-22"^^xsd:date ;
    ontosage:answerText "Accessible WC on Floor 0 (Ground Floor). Inspected and confirmed working." ;
    ontosage:isSimulated true .

